Strength Score Reference Table

Strength Label	Score	Rules Passed	What It Means
Very Weak	1	0–1 or common	Dangerously weak; guessable in seconds
Weak	2	2	Minimal variety; easily cracked
Fair	3	3	Acceptable but improvable
Strong	4	4	Good with one small gap
Very Strong	5	5	All rules passed; recommended

Why the Program Produces Correct Results
1.	Regular expressions are exact — re.search() never misses a character or returns a false positive for well-defined character classes like [A-Z] or [0-9].
2.	sum(rules) is mathematically sound because Python guarantees True == 1 and False == 0 across all versions.
3.	The common-password override runs first, preventing a false sense of security from passwords like 'Password1!' which technically passes four rules but appears in every hacker wordlist.
4.	getpass.getpass() suppresses echo at the OS level, not just the Python level — the password is never written to the terminal buffer, so it cannot be captured by screen-recording tools.

